{
  "openresult": "1.0",
  "title": "A mass finish given the same time",
  "lang": "en",
  "description": "Eighteen riders credited with the same time, which is what a mass finish publishes. Nothing but §8.5.3's stable sort decides their order. Eighteen and not three because the number is measured: Ruby's sort preserves order at seven elements and reorders at twelve, and until this case the largest results array in the whole suite was seven — so a consumer on a runtime without a stable sort earned a clean conformance run and reordered a mass finish in production.",
